SQS: queue model
sns: pub/sub model
kinesis: real-time streaming model

producer sends message in to sqs queue
consumers poll message from a queue
queue: is a list of tasks that need to be done
SQS: fully managed service this means that the applications are decoupled
producer -> SDK protocol -> queue -> poll SQS messages -> consumer
deleteMessageAPI prevents messages from being in the queue by deleting the messages that are pulled

a way to do it in real life:

SQS queue 
              -> poll for messages 
              -> EC2 instances
SQS queue     
              -> cloudwatch metric for queue length 
              -> alarm for breach 
              -> cloudwatch alarm 
              -> ASG/Auto scaling group which is connected to EC2 instances
encryption:
  -> in-flight: https api
  -> at-rest:kms keys
  -> client side: encryption/decryption client
Access control: IAM policies
message visibility timeout: if message pulled by consumer it becomes invisible to other consumer
changeMessageVisibility: helps change the time of how long the message is not visible for other cosumers

